 "intro_html": "Measure thickness, not weight. This page uses ChefSteps’ <b><span class=\"q\" data-k=\"temp\" data-u=\"C\" data-a=\"50\" data-s=\"0\">50 °C</span> soft-salmon method</b>, with a separate estimate for frozen portions. For other sizes and the firmer <span class=\"q\" data-k=\"temp\" data-u=\"C\" data-a=\"60\" data-s=\"0\">60 °C</span> pasteurized option, see the <a href=\"sous-vide.html#salmon\">salmon reference table</a>.",
 "mise": [],
 "more_label": "More sous vide:",
 "next": {
  "slug": "sous-vide-fries",
  "title": "Brined sous vide French fries"
 },
 "notes": [
  {
   "html": "<ul class=\"do\"><li>Use salmon suitable for undercooked service with supplier-confirmed parasite controls.</li><li>Ordinary freezer storage does not prove parasite destruction.</li><li>This unpasteurized preparation is unsuitable for pregnant or immunocompromised people; choose a fully cooked option instead.</li></ul>",
   "title_html": "Choosing salmon for 50 °C"
  },
  {
   "html": "<ul class=\"do\"><li>For chilled salmon, Baldwin’s fatty-fish table at <b><span class=\"q\" data-k=\"temp\" data-u=\"C\" data-a=\"60\" data-s=\"0\">60 °C</span></b> includes both heating and bacterial reduction: <span class=\"q\" data-k=\"len\" data-u=\"mm\" data-a=\"20\" data-s=\"0\">20 mm</span> → 75 min; <span class=\"q\" data-k=\"len\" data-u=\"mm\" data-a=\"25\" data-s=\"0\">25 mm</span> → 90 min; <span class=\"q\" data-k=\"len\" data-u=\"mm\" data-a=\"30\" data-s=\"0\">30 mm</span> → 120 min.</li><li>Do not apply these chilled times directly to frozen fish.</li><li>Thaw in the fridge first, removing reduced-oxygen retail packaging before thawing.</li></ul>",
   "title_html": "Firmer, pasteurized salmon"
  },
  {
   "html": "<ul class=\"do\"><li>Use the <a href=\"sous-vide.html#thickness\">thickness calculator</a> for the same soft-salmon schedule.</li><li>It keeps salmon timings separate from meat heating estimates.</li></ul>",
   "title_html": "Thickness calculator"
  }
 ],
