   "title": "Cook at 50 °C",
   "uses_rows": []
  },
  {
   "body_html": "<ul class=\"do\"><li>Lift the fish out carefully with a fish spatula and pat dry. Skinless salmon can go straight to the plate.</li><li>For skin-on portions, heat the neutral oil in a pan and sear <b>skin-side down</b> until crisp, about <b>30–60 seconds</b>. Keep the flesh intact; avoid a long second cook.</li></ul>",
